{
  "_about": "The bar's menu: the spirits, liqueurs and aperitifs by the pour, the wine list, the sake, the cocktails and the beer prices. bar.py adds it to the menu after the GloriaFood export (gloriafood.py), cooked at the bar station and taxed as alcohol. A category is a shelf or a page of the printed menu, with the optional choices in its groups; an item sells in its sizes, or in the category's pour (the default one is the 1.5 oz pour) at its price. A category marked existing is one the export already has: its items join that category after the export's own. prices are the printed menu's prices for the export's own items. A new hub seeds its database from this file; a running hub takes additions, and the prices where the editor has not changed them, with `hubctl menu import --apply`; everything else changes through the menu editor. Pour prices (Nov 2026): the 750 mL retail price in the Boston area / 16.9 pours of 1.5 oz / 20% pour cost, rounded to the nearest .45 or .95, never below 7.95 (7.45 for well brands and cordials); retail_750 records that basis. Wine, sake, cocktail and beer prices are the printed menu's. An item with \"visible\": false stays in the catalog but off the order screen.",
